A: Can you read a whole Russian story on your own, again? This one has ten sentences.
    draw open_rest open_cat parallel true

    erase open_rest open_cat

A: Every word in it comes from lessons one to nineteen: read it first, and tap any word you're unsure of.
    draw s1 s2 s3 s4 s5 s6 s7

B: Сего́дня суббо́та. Ма́ша и Том в рестора́не.
    highlight s1_words color #c9871a

B: Рестора́н но́вый и большо́й.
    highlight s2_words color #c9871a

B: Том хо́чет ко́фе, а Ма́ша хо́чет во́ду.
    highlight s3_words color #c9871a

B: Ко́фе сто́ит сто рубле́й.
    highlight s4_words color #c9871a

B: Кто э́то на окне́? Коты́!
    highlight s5_words color #c9871a

B: Ма́ша говори́т: «Мне нра́вятся коты́!»
    highlight s6_words color #c9871a

B: Вчера́ Ма́ша была́ на мо́ре. Том то́же был там.
    highlight s7_words color #c9871a

A: Сего́дня суббо́та, today is Saturday, is from lesson fifteen; and в рестора́не, in a restaurant, from lesson nine.
    highlight s1_words color #c9871a

B: Рестора́н is он, so new and big take his endings: но́вый, and большо́й, with its stressed -ой.
    highlight s2_w_2 s2_w_4 color #2f6b8f effect pulse

A: Хо́чет, wants, is lesson thirteen's: Tom wants coffee, and ко́фе never changes.
    highlight s3_w_2 s3_w_3 color #c9871a effect pulse

B: And Masha wants во́ду, water: вода́ takes the object ending у, as after ви́жу.
    highlight s3_w_7 color #3f7d4e part у$ effect pulse

A: Then the price, from lesson sixteen: ко́фе сто́ит сто рубле́й, coffee costs a hundred roubles.
    highlight s4_words color #c9871a

B: Кто э́то на окне́? Who is that on the windowsill? Кто, not что, because in Russian a cat is a who.
    highlight s5_w_1 color #c9871a

A: Коты́, cats: кот with the ы of lesson eleven, and many cats are они́.
    highlight s5_w_5 color #4f8a3c part ы effect pulse

B: Мне нра́вятся коты́: I like cats, or really, cats please me. Many cats, so нра́вятся, not нра́вится.
    highlight s6_w_4 color #4f8a3c part ятся$ effect pulse

A: Last, вчера́, yesterday: Ма́ша была́ на мо́ре, Masha was at the seaside, with the а of a she.
    highlight s7_w_3 color #b5482e part а$ effect pulse

B: And Том то́же был там: Tom was there too, and был, for a he, has no ending.
    highlight s7_w_8 color #2f6b8f effect pulse

    hide story s1_g_1 s1_g_2 s1_g_3 s1_g_4 s1_g_5 s1_g_6 s1_g_7 s2_g_1 s2_g_2 s2_g_3 s2_g_4 s3_g_1 s3_g_2 s3_g_3 s3_g_4 s3_g_5 s3_g_6 s3_g_7 s4_g_1 s4_g_2 s4_g_3 s4_g_4 s5_g_1 s5_g_2 s5_g_3 s5_g_4 s5_g_5 s6_g_1 s6_g_2 s6_g_3 s6_g_4 s6_g_5 s7_g_1 s7_g_2 s7_g_3 s7_g_4 s7_g_5 s7_g_6 s7_g_7 s7_g_8 s7_g_9

    quiz "What day is it in the story? Pick one." reveal.text "Сего́дня суббо́та." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 420 reveal.style label reveal.size 72 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        intro: Now five questions on the story, from memory.
        right: Saturday: the story's very first words.
        wrong: Look back at the first line: сего́дня… which day?
        * понеде́льник
        + суббо́та
        * пя́тница

    erase reveal_1_stamp

    quiz "What does Masha want? Pick one." reveal.text "Ма́ша хо́чет во́ду." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 420 reveal.style label reveal.size 72 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Water, with the object ending; Tom has the coffee.
        wrong: Tom has the coffee; look at the second half of line three.
        * ко́фе
        * чай
        + во́ду

    erase reveal_2_stamp

    ask "How much is the coffee? Type the number in Russian." answer ["сто","сто рублей"] reveal.text "сто рубле́й" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 420 reveal.style label reveal.size 72 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        keys: АБВГДЕЁЖЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУФХЦЧШЩЪЫЬЭЮЯ
        right: A hundred: ко́фе сто́ит сто рубле́й.
        wrong: Three letters, and more than пятьдеся́т.

    erase reveal_3_stamp

    quiz "Кто на окне́? Who is on the windowsill? Pick one." reveal.text "на окне́ коты́" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 420 reveal.style label reveal.size 72 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: The cats, and they're a кто, not a что.
        wrong: Line five: кто э́то на окне́? …
        * ма́ма
        + коты́
        * мой брат

    erase reveal_4_stamp

    quiz "Где была́ Ма́ша вчера́? Where was Masha yesterday? Pick one." reveal.text "на мо́ре" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 420 reveal.style label reveal.size 72 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        right: At the seaside, and Tom was there too.
        wrong: The last line: вчера́ Ма́ша была́ на… what?
        * в рестора́не
        * в до́ме
        + на мо́ре

    erase reveal_5_stamp

    draw score_win

    draw score_cat1 score_cat2 parallel true

A: You got {t1.score} of {t1.total}.
    results test t1 retry true pass 4

    erase score_cat1 score_cat2 score_win

    draw grid

A: Now look back at lessons eleven to nineteen. You can say more than one, and make new and big agree with their noun.
    highlight L11 L12 color #c9871a effect pulse

B: You can say what you want and what you see, name the day, and ask what it costs.
    highlight L13 L14 L15 L16 color #c9871a effect pulse

A: You can ask who, what and when, say where you were yesterday, and say what you like.
    highlight L17 L18 L19 color #c9871a effect pulse

B: And you've just read ten sentences on your own: not one word in them was new.
    highlight L20 color #c9871a

    erase grid

B: Спаси́бо! Пока́!
    draw end_tom end_masha parallel true

